    {
      "id": 879614,
      "category": "researcher",
      "content": "The IBM watsonx.data MCP server exposes Streamable HTTP at `/mcp` without an inbound caller secret or effective Host/Origin validation. A malicious web page can use DNS rebinding to keep the attacker origin while its hostname resolves to `127.0.0.1`, initialize the local MCP session, enumerate tools, and invoke watsonx.data-backed tools through the server-held IBM IAM credential path. The attached demo uses fake watsonx.data data, but it runs the genuine upstream MCP server path and proves the browser-origin request reaches tool dispatch and the server-held backend authorization path.\n{F6306137}",
      "updated_at": "2026-07-23T10:15:11.506Z",
      "can_view?": true,
      "can_create?": false,
